# Real environment files. `.env.example` is committed on purpose — it is the
# documentation — and the mode-specific `.env.production` style files are not
# ignored either, since those are the intended way to commit a *public* setting.
# What must never be committed is a machine-specific value or a secret.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

